# Mandare guardrail

Never use network access to obtain implementation details when the repository
already contains the relevant source, tests, schemas, or documentation. Prefer
repository evidence over external evidence.

## Practice

- Search and read in-repo paths first (`src/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, `spec/`,
  `config/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/skills/`).
- Use `WebFetch` only when the user supplies a URL, or when the repo clearly
  lacks the needed contract/docs and a listed domain is required.
- Do not use open-ended web search for Mandare implementation work; it introduces
  non-deterministic external context that weakens replay and evidence quality.
- When external material is used, cite the URL and state why in-repo evidence
  was insufficient.
